rah|a|Pertaining to a league or treaty; derived from an agreement or covenant between parties, especially between nations; constituted by a compact between parties, usually governments or their representatives. ; Composed of states or districts which retain only a subordinate and limited sovereignty, as the Union of the United States, or the Sonderbund of Switzerland. ; Consisting or pertaining to such a government; as, the Federal Constitution; a Federal officer. ; Friendly or devoted to such a government; as, the Federal party. see Federalist.	j:zue,71,6;231i,71,6;1ptr,66,2;1p20,62,3;1p3q,61,2;1mh,59,2;vi3,58,16;g8w,58,4;1lnt,57,4;1si,53,4~tpa,37,20;vi3,58,16;15h0,46,11;1yhg,7,7;125p,48,7;1xja,31,6;231i,71,6;1jyl,31,6;zue,71,6;xzf,36,5
