ras|n|property; possession; tenure. ; Reward or compensation for services rendered or to be rendered; especially, payment for professional services, of optional amount, or fixed by custom or laws; charge; pay; perquisite; as, the fees of lawyers and physicians; the fees of office; clerk's fees; sheriff's fees; marriage fees, etc. ; A right to the use of a superior's land, as a stipend for services to be performed; also, the land so held; a fief. ; An estate of inheritance supposed to be held either mediately or immediately from the sovereign, and absolutely vested in the owner. ; An estate of inheritance belonging to the owner, and transmissible to his heirs, absolutely and simply, without condition attached to the tenure.	a:qa7,87,3;x7p,82,4;1pi4,80,3;1cq4,71,7;1asb,50,3;3a3,45,3;s34,41,5;1oss,38,2;247g,32,3;22vf,31,3~tml,28,13;1vhw,20,9;1cq4,71,7;zw,22,6;s34,41,5;qmh,19,5;x7p,82,4;22vf,31,3;3a3,45,3;1mob,13,3	v:f62,43,3;1p29,28,1;1gz1,14,3~f62,43,3;1gz1,14,3;1p29,28,1	V:27xf,73,6;27xg,68,2;521,41,3;1gz6,40,6;133c,14,2;6g5,7,3~27xf,73,6;1gz6,40,6;6g5,7,3;521,41,3;27xg,68,2;133c,14,2	n:18uf,67,8;op7,67,5;1p29,66,14;28zu,63,4;247g,55,15;161i,55,2;1gn8,55,5;1ywm,51,3;tp3,48,5;pxe,44,3~enw,32,16;247g,55,15;1p29,66,14;1mo2,25,12;42p,28,11;290l,1,8;18uf,67,8;hi,20,5;1gn8,55,5;op7,67,5	N:2879,105,3;27xh,77,10;51g,41,2;1gz8,33,1~27xh,77,10;2879,105,3;51g,41,2;1gz8,33,1
